    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 1,
      "sourceSentenceId": 1,
      "chunkId": "s45-p01",
      "image": "assets/images/01.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p01.mp3",
      "en": "What would happen if you tried to blow a soap bubble in below freezing weather?",
      "cn": "如果你在零度以下的天气里吹肥皂泡，会发生什么呢？"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 2,
      "sourceSentenceId": 2,
      "chunkId": "s45-p02",
      "image": "assets/images/02.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p02.mp3",
      "en": "Would it freeze and fall to the ground?",
      "cn": "它会冻住，然后掉到地上吗？"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 3,
      "sourceSentenceId": 3,
      "chunkId": "s45-p03",
      "image": "assets/images/03.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p03.mp3",
      "en": "Would you have to hit it with a stone to break it?",
      "cn": "你是不是得用石头砸才能把它弄破呢？"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 4,
      "sourceSentenceId": 4,
      "chunkId": "s45-p04",
      "image": "assets/images/04.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p04.mp3",
      "en": "These questions came into my mind one cold winter day as I finished my freshly baked apple pie.",
      "cn": "在一个寒冷的冬天，当我吃完刚出炉的苹果派时，这些问题浮现在我的脑海里。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 5,
      "sourceSentenceId": 5,
      "chunkId": "s45-p05",
      "image": "assets/images/05.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p05.mp3",
      "en": "It was a perfect time to experiment with blowing frozen bubbles.",
      "cn": "那时正是做吹冰冻泡泡实验的好时机。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 6,
      "sourceSentenceId": 6,
      "chunkId": "s45-p06-01",
      "image": "assets/images/06.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p06-01.mp3",
      "en": "To blow frozen bubbles, I had to wait until the air outside was very cold,",
      "cn": "为了吹出冰冻泡泡，我得等到室外空气非常寒冷，"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 7,
      "sourceSentenceId": 6,
      "chunkId": "s45-p06-02",
      "image": "assets/images/06.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p06-02.mp3",
      "en": "meaning 10 degrees below zero Fahrenheit or colder.",
      "cn": "也就是零下10华氏度（约零下23摄氏度）或更冷的时候。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 8,
      "sourceSentenceId": 7,
      "chunkId": "s45-p07",
      "image": "assets/images/07.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p07.mp3",
      "en": "I didn't have the bubble things that come in a bottle, so I used dish-washing soap.",
      "cn": "我没有瓶装的泡泡水，于是用了洗洁精。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 9,
      "sourceSentenceId": 8,
      "chunkId": "s45-p08",
      "image": "assets/images/08.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p08.mp3",
      "en": "I chose a place out of the wind, and blew bubbles the same way I always do.",
      "cn": "我选了一个避风的地方，像往常一样吹泡泡。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 10,
      "sourceSentenceId": 9,
      "chunkId": "s45-p09",
      "image": "assets/images/09.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p09.mp3",
      "en": "Here's what I learned.",
      "cn": "以下是我的发现。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 11,
      "sourceSentenceId": 10,
      "chunkId": "s45-p10",
      "image": "assets/images/10.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p10.mp3",
      "en": "If the temperature is low enough, the skin of the bubble frosts over, becoming cloudy instead of clear.",
      "cn": "如果温度足够低，泡泡的表面会结霜，变得浑浊而不是透明。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 12,
      "sourceSentenceId": 11,
      "chunkId": "s45-p11",
      "image": "assets/images/11.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p11.mp3",
      "en": "And what about those rainbow swirls that you see in soap bubbles?",
      "cn": "那么你在肥皂泡中看到的那些彩虹漩涡呢？"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 13,
      "sourceSentenceId": 12,
      "chunkId": "s45-p12",
      "image": "assets/images/12.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p12.mp3",
      "en": "The rainbow colours stay even when the bubbles frost, but they don't spin any more.",
      "cn": "即便泡泡结霜，彩虹的颜色依然存在，但它们不再旋转。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 14,
      "sourceSentenceId": 13,
      "chunkId": "s45-p13",
      "image": "assets/images/13.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p13.mp3",
      "en": "The bubbles still float in the air.",
      "cn": "泡泡仍然漂浮在空中。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 15,
      "sourceSentenceId": 14,
      "chunkId": "s45-p14",
      "image": "assets/images/14.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p14.mp3",
      "en": "They don't fall to the ground any faster than they would on a summer day.",
      "cn": "它们落到地面的速度并不比在夏天时更快。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 16,
      "sourceSentenceId": 15,
      "chunkId": "s45-p15",
      "image": "assets/images/15.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p15.mp3",
      "en": "When these bubbles break, they don't turn into tiny drops of soap.",
      "cn": "当这些泡泡破裂时，它们不会变成微小的肥皂液滴。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 17,
      "sourceSentenceId": 16,
      "chunkId": "s45-p16",
      "image": "assets/images/16.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p16.mp3",
      "en": "They turn into shiny rainbow-coloured pieces and fly slowly to the ground.",
      "cn": "它们会变成闪亮的彩虹色碎片，慢慢飘落到地上。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 18,
      "sourceSentenceId": 17,
      "chunkId": "s45-p17",
      "image": "assets/images/17.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p17.mp3",
      "en": "Sometimes a frozen bubble will roll across the snow without breaking.",
      "cn": "有时，一个冰冻泡泡会在雪地上滚动且不破裂。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 19,
      "sourceSentenceId": 18,
      "chunkId": "s45-p18",
      "image": "assets/images/18.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s45-p18.mp3",
      "en": "If it breaks, it may leave a strong bubble skin on the ground.",
      "cn": "如果它破裂了，可能会在地面上留下一层坚固的泡泡膜。"
    }
  ]
